ed `fund_live_shrimp_biomass` (reserve-only, no dissolved pool fallback) places reproduction near the boundary of feasibility in this test fixture. The fixture starts with reserve_g=0.0 and must accumulate enough reserve over 60 simulated days via feeding before hatching can succeed. If the test is sensitive to build environment or execution order, it may fail intermittently in CI. Consider either (a) seeding `state.animal.reserve_g` with a modest initial value in `shrimp_reproduction_budget_state` to provide margin, or (b) adding a diagnostic assertion that logs accumulated reserve before the hatching assertion to aid debugging if flakiness recurs.","rationale":"A test that fails intermittently is worse than one that fails consistently because it erodes CI trust and is hard to debug. Since the behavioral change (removing dissolved pool fallback) narrows the conditions under which reproduction succeeds, the test fixture should be updated to have clear margin above the new threshold."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"7236b8cf-a221-4605-a139-63252f69f1c8"}
